From: hoangvu12 <hggaming91@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 04:06:02 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Live chat between the person's computers goes direct:
 replies, sends, steers, wakes and catch-up

A reply streaming in a chat on another of the person's computers reached
them only through the edge's ChatRoom, and their sends, steers and wakes
reached its host the same way.

- A device viewing a relayed chat opens a live chat link to its host
  (WatchChatLink, SendChatFrames; chat-link-v1) on a road other than the
  relay that proved this device. A second path only: the ChatRoom stays
  the record; direct frames never become rows or move a cursor.
- Sends and steers go both ways and run once (the command ledger); a cold
  chat's host is woken directly (WakeChat), the edge's nudge the backup.
- A device back on a chat catches up from its host over the link; while
  the room stays out of reach, the host's answer settles a reopen.
- One check for who may call direct (direct_peer); the relay refuses
  these calls (direct_only); caps of 4 per chat, 8 per device, 32 in all.
- Roads: an ordered list, each with its own health. A cut-off read is
  asked again on a fresh link, then on the next road, within one
  deadline; with the edge known down, not on the relay. A dialled link
  closes once its device may no longer be reached, or after an hour; a
  busy or refusing far end is waited out briefly; a served link cut off
  ends the calls and streams on it, and types no terminal input it had
  queued.
- Test harness: tests/support (fake edge, Gate, log capture, pairing both
  ways), mock-server's down/held RegistryRoom, #[doc(hidden)]
  set_presence_timing and registry_pending_len.

Tests: chat_relay's 9 new, chat_client's 1 new, chat_direct's 9,
chat_catch_up's 4, test_seams' 7, direct_peer's 5, chat_link's 3,
room_down's 2, direct_only's 1, next_road's 7, direct_rpc's 9 new,
zeron-rpc server's 3 new.
